  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> be two real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If the complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is of unit modulus and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></math> lies on the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then a possible value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> is greatest integer function, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
